{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C8wSTYrcvRrGTfLSGgc7nJ","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"id\": \"E04.3\",\n  \"check\": \"Metadata the scanner flags is cleaned or rejected, not just logged.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Open the scanner's result handling. 2) Check flagged metadata is cleaned, or the tool rejected, before the model sees it. 3) Answer no if flagged items are only logged or warned about and passed through.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E04.4\",\n  \"check\": \"A scanner error or outage blocks the metadata instead of letting it through unchecked.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"verify\": \"1) Read every `try/except`, `catch`, and timeout around the scanner call. 2) Check an error blocks the metadata. 3) Answer no if any error branch passes metadata through, returns clean, or skips the scan, or a config flag disables scanning by default.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E04.1\",\n  \"check\": \"A scanner runs on server instructions, tool names, titles, descriptions, input and output schemas, annotations, and prompt and resource templates before the model sees them.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"fields\": [\n    \"server_instructions\",\n    \"tool_names\",\n    \"tool_titles\",\n    \"tool_descriptions\",\n    \"input_schemas\",\n    \"output_schemas\",\n    \"annotations\",\n    \"prompt_templates\",\n    \"resource_templates\"\n  ],\n  \"rules\": [\n    \"hidden_instructions\",\n    \"cross_tool_references\",\n    \"control_characters\",\n    \"role_overrides\",\n    \"encoded_payloads\",\n    \"data_sending_targets\",\n    \"length_limits\"\n  ],\n  \"attempt_categories\": [\n    \"field_differential\"\n  ],\n  \"verify\": \"1) Inventory every model-visible metadata field and loading path. 2) Build a field-by-rule matrix: names, titles, descriptions, schemas, annotations, instructions, prompts and resource templates. 3) For each field, trace the actual scanner rules applied before serialization to the model. A syntax regex alone is not proof that payload/instruction rules ran. 4) Try the same suspicious string in different fields; answer no for an unscanned required surface.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"E04.2\",\n  \"check\": \"The scanner checks for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and data-sending targets, and enforces length limits.\",\n  \"coverage_required\": true,\n  \"attempt_categories\": [\n    \"encoded_payload\",\n    \"multiline_override\"\n  ],\n  \"verify\": \"1) Trace rule application, not just rule declarations. 2) Attempt encoded strings and multi-line role overrides; record input, exact code path and outcome. 3) Verify hidden instructions, cross-tool references, control/invisible characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, data-sending targets and length limits. 4) Answer no when a required rule is absent or a demonstrated suspicious input bypasses it.\",\n  \"candidate_sites\": []\n}\nusage: answer.py [-h] [--repo REPO] [--met {yes,no,unknown}] [--evidence EVIDENCE] [--quote QUOTE] [--counter COUNTER] [--note NOTE]\n                 [--rating {likely_pass,gap,needs_evidence,na_candidate}] [--confidence {high,medium,low}] [--summary SUMMARY] [--next NEXT_STEP] [--violates VIOLATES]\n                 [--also-affects ALSO_AFFECTS] [--verdict {confirmed,dismissed}] [--item ITEM] [--reason REASON]\n                 findings {check,flag,item,prescan,next} [target]\n\nWrite one answer into a findings file, check it, and show what's next.\n\nUse this instead of editing the JSON by hand.\n\n  Answer a check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json check B05.2 --met no --evidence src/x.py:41 \\\n        --quote \"exact code on that line\" --note \"what the code does\" [--counter \"what you searched\"]\n\n  Add a red flag:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json flag B05 --evidence src/x.py:41 --note \"what's wrong\"\n\n  Finish an item:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json item B05 --rating gap --confidence high \\\n        --summary \"one sentence\" --next \"what to fix\" [--violates \"exact words from the requirement\"] \\\n        [--also-affects E06]\n\n  Resolve a pre-scan hit:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json prescan H003 --verdict confirmed --item R03 --reason \"...\"\n\n  Show the next unanswered check:\n    python answer.py FINDINGS.json next\n\nThe quote is checked against the file right away; a \"yes\" without a matching quote\nand a counter-search is refused. Paths are relative to the repo, which defaults to the\nfolder holding FINDINGS.json (set --repo to change it).\n\npositional arguments:\n  findings\n  {check,flag,item,prescan,next}\n  target\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --repo REPO\n  --met {yes,no,unknown}\nusage: review_coverage.py [-h] {inventory,policy,ledger} ...\n\nStatic candidate inventory and evidence ledger. Never executes repository code.\n\npython review_coverage.py inventory REPO\npython review_coverage.py ledger FINDINGS.json CHECK --rows rows.json --attempts attempts.json\n\nInventory matches are candidates, not findings or proof of completeness. Review\naliases, wrappers, computed calls and unsupported languages manually as well.\n\npositional arguments:\n  {inventory,policy,ledger}\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n438:  \"prescan_resolutions\": {}\n{\n  \"sites\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"If7878f59fe\",\n      \"kind\": \"tool_registration\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/agent/budget.ts:165\",\n      \"quote\": \"const r = await this.store.add(key, amount, max, ttl);\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I11c134ddd9\",\n      \"kind\": \"model_call\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/agent/classifier.ts:45\",\n      \"quote\": \"res = await client.messages.create(\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I1ae2dd3bba\",\n      \"kind\": \"a